// History Claims: popular claims that a verse matches the ancient record, checked one by one.
// Verse text is NOT stored here. Cards read it live from corpus.js (QURAN_VERSES) and translation_en.js (QURAN_EN) by key.
// Years are numbers (negative = BCE). lost = last year the record could be read (null = never lost before the revelation).
// verdict: 'holds' | 'partial' | 'weak' (how well the claim as stated survives the evidence). card_* is the one-line answer on the index.
// region: 'egypt' | 'arabia' | 'neareast'. To add a claim, add an entry with the same shape.
// videos: where the claim circulates (YouTube id, t = start in seconds, short: true for a Short). Each was checked against its transcript.
// diff_*: how the videos tell it differently from the summary. acc_*: replaces the timeline sentence when there is no written record.

